A||||3||DaveL||Throttle Valve Cable||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||12-10-2000||08:32 AM||||Well, I've been trying to readjust my throttle valve cable, but there isn't any sort of button on the damn thing. (87 SE 2.5 DIS A/T) Maybe some one put some sort of aftermarket cable on it....? There is a sort of junction at the transmission end of the cable, but no external button of any sort. There is a male and a female end that plug together, held by 2 little tangs (tangs?). I took this partially apart, and there seems to be no way to adjust it.  help||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||12-10-2000||08:42 AM||||The adjustment is at the throttle boby end. There is a metal tab that is fairly difficult to press. I believe the tab is "D" shaped. When you press it, the cable should slide within its own mounting.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||afRaceR||12-10-2000||05:54 PM||||Rockcrawl is exactly right, the button is at the throttle body side and it is "D" shaped. It takes a little pressure to push it in.<P>Here's how to adjust your cable, Press the button and let the cable pull all the way in, sit in your car and push the peddle all the way to the floor with some pressure. Test drive and see how that works, if its still alittle off, grab the cable end at the throttle body and pull on it until it clicks one time, test drive again. <P>This should be enough to adjust it if your transmission is in good shape. If its still not right you may have more problems like sticky valves or governor or worse.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-10-2000||11:28 PM||||87-88 DIS 4 cyl TV cable DOES NOT work like the older ones.<P>The cable adjuster IS ON THE TRANSMISSION END! Not the TBI end. It is a Square button on the side of the fat part of the cable. The button is not raised above the cable shell. The button shell looks like someone stuck a block in the middle of the cable.<P>You press the button and pull the cable ABOVE the adjuster button OUT of the tranny. The lower fat section DOES NOT MOVE. DO NOT press the accelerator pedal to make this adjustment. Turn the black pully next to the TBI CCW untill the TBI is at or as close to WOT as you can get it.<P>Make sure you don't pull out the cable too far. Not more then a 1/4 inch should be needed unless the cable has a problem. If the button pops up above the shell or is crooked then the cable has been pulled to far. depress the button and return it into the tranny by hand untill the button sets at it's normal hight.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-10-2000).]||||reg||1
